@using Microsoft.Extensions.Localization

@inject IStringLocalizerFactory _stringLocalizerFactory

@{
    IStringLocalizer localizer = _stringLocalizerFactory.Create("Lumina.Presentation.Web.Views.Shared._Layout", "Lumina.Presentation.Web");
}

@*
    APPLICATION FALLBACK AUDIO PLAYER BAR - READ BEFORE EDITING

    This partial renders the audio player bar into the fallback layout of the application, for an authenticated visitor.
    The themed layout renders the same bar from the 'shared/audio-player' template of the active theme instead, and only
    calls this partial when the theme does not provide one. Either way, the markup is only the structure: the behavior
    lives in the global audio player script (wwwroot/js/audio-player/), which binds to the hooks documented below.

    The bar is hidden by default. The 'hidden' attribute keeps it unrendered until the audio player script takes over,
    so a page load never shows the bar, not even for a frame while the stylesheets settle. The script then hands the bar
    to the 'not-shown' class, which keeps it hidden until playback starts.

    The DOM contract a theme must preserve is:
      - The container element with the 'audio-player-container' class, carrying 'not-shown' while the bar is hidden,
        and 'expanded' while it is expanded. The audio player toggles both classes. While the bar is hidden the player
        also sets the 'inert' attribute on it, and removes it when the bar is shown, so a collapsed bar keeps none of
        its focusable controls in the tab order. The position and orientation of the container are entirely theme-owned:
        this fallback stylesheet uses a flex column with the bar at the bottom, but a theme may place the bar vertically
        on a side and expand its queue horizontally.
      - The main content element, carrying 'audio-player-not-shown' while the bar is hidden, and
        'audio-player-bar-expanded' while it is expanded. The audio player toggles these classes on it as well.
      - The element with the id 'audio-player-expand-toggle', which the global site script binds and routes to the audio player.
      - The hook attributes the audio player binds: 'data-audio-player-play-pause', '-stop', '-previous', '-next', '-repeat',
        '-progress', '-progress-played', '-progress-downloaded', '-progress-undownloaded', '-current-time', '-total-time',
        '-track-name', '-album-name', '-now-playing-title', '-now-playing-release-type', '-now-playing-release',
        '-now-playing-year', '-now-playing-artist', '-artwork-carousel', '-cover-thumbnail', '-cover-image', '-volume', '-volume-level', '-mute', '-queue', '-playlist-combobox' and '-add-queue-to-playlist'.
        The queue-to-playlist action is a standard application combo box, so a theme renders the usual 'enlightenment-combobox'
        markup and puts the '-playlist-combobox' hook on its root. The player only reads the 'data-value' of the selected text
        when the add button is pressed. A theme that renders one half of the action gets a complete built-in pair, placed in a
        queue area wrapper above the queue so that it never becomes a new column of the expanded layout.
        The volume fill element ('-volume-level') is a styling hook the stylesheet drives from the custom properties below,
        not one the script writes to. The repeat toggle carries 'data-audio-player-repeat' and the player writes
        'data-audio-player-repeat-mode' ('off', 'all' or 'one') and toggles the 'is-active' and 'is-one' classes on it.
        A queue item root rendered by the player always carries 'data-audio-player-queue-entry-id', whether it comes from the
        theme sub template or from the built-in markup, so clicking it starts that entry. The queue element stays the scroll
        container of the list, because the player scrolls the current entry to the start of whichever axis the theme makes
        scrollable when playback advances or the bar expands.
      - The three state progress bar: the played part carries 'audio-player-progress-played', the downloaded but not
        played part carries 'audio-player-progress-downloaded', and the not yet downloaded part carries
        'audio-player-progress-undownloaded'. Each layer also carries 'data-audio-player-progress-layer' ('played',
        'downloaded' or 'undownloaded') in the markup, so a theme can select a layer by state as well as by class. The
        player publishes the start and the width of each state as the CSS custom properties
        '--audio-player-progress-played-start', '-played-width', '-downloaded-start', '-downloaded-width',
        '-undownloaded-start' and '-undownloaded-width' on the bar, and the volume fill as
        '--audio-player-volume-start' and '--audio-player-volume-width' on the volume control, and writes no inline
        geometry, so a theme consumes the properties to style each state and to give either bar its own shape and
        orientation. The player marks the bar with 'is-buffering' while it is loading, and carries the state in
        'data-audio-player-progress-state' ('idle', 'ready' or 'buffering') together with the slider ARIA attributes.
      - Themed shells only: the plain text script elements that carry the raw source of the
        'shared/audio-player/queue-item' and 'shared/audio-player/playlist-item' sub templates, with the ids
        'audio-player-template-queue-item' and 'audio-player-template-playlist-item'. This application fallback partial
        renders neither element; it intentionally uses the built-in queue item markup.

    The play affordances the pages hand to the player use the 'data-audio-player-play' trigger attribute, a shuffled play
    affordance uses 'data-audio-player-play-shuffled' together with 'data-audio-player-shuffle-scope' ('release', 'artist' or
    'library'), a whole library play affordance uses 'data-audio-player-play-library' with 'data-library-id', a whole library
    shuffle affordance uses 'data-audio-player-play-library-shuffled' with 'data-library-id', and a play next affordance uses
    'data-audio-player-play-next'. A track trigger must carry libraryId, trackId, albumId and artistId, because the playback
    manifest route needs all four Ids. The 'Play Affordances on the Music Pages' section of
    docs/technical/theming/Theming.md documents this contract for theme authors.
*@

<div class="audio-player-container not-shown" hidden>
    <!-- Expanded area: current track details and album artwork beside the current queue, including a single track. -->
    <div class="audio-player-expanded">
        <div class="audio-player-now-playing">
            <img class="audio-player-cover-image" data-audio-player-cover-image alt="" />
            <div class="audio-player-now-playing-labels">
                <span class="audio-player-now-playing-title" data-audio-player-now-playing-title></span>
                <div class="audio-player-now-playing-release-line">
                    <span class="audio-player-now-playing-release-type" data-audio-player-now-playing-release-type></span>
                    <span class="audio-player-now-playing-release" data-audio-player-now-playing-release></span>
                    <span class="audio-player-now-playing-year" data-audio-player-now-playing-year></span>
                </div>
                <span class="audio-player-now-playing-artist" data-audio-player-now-playing-artist></span>
            </div>
            <div class="audio-player-artwork-carousel artwork-carousel" data-audio-player-artwork-carousel role="group" aria-label="@localizer["AudioPlayerAlbumArtwork"]" hidden></div>
        </div>
        <div class="audio-player-queue-area">
            <div class="audio-player-queue-actions">
                <div class="enlightenment-combobox audio-player-queue-playlist-combobox" id="audio-player-playlist-combobox" data-audio-player-playlist-combobox>
                    <div class="shine-effect" style="top: 1px;"></div>
                    <input type="checkbox" class="enlightenment-toggle-checkbox" id="audio-player-playlist-combobox-toggle" />
                    <label class="enlightenment-toggle" for="audio-player-playlist-combobox-toggle">
                        <span class="enlightenment-selected-text" data-value="">@localizer["AudioPlayerSelectPlaylist"]</span>
                    </label>
                    <div class="enlightenment-dropdown" id="audio-player-playlist-combobox-dropdown">
                        <div class="shine-effect" style="top: -4px;"></div>
                        <div class="enlightenment-option first-option disabled">@localizer["AudioPlayerSelectPlaylist"]</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <button type="button" class="confirm-button h-22px audio-player-add-queue-to-playlist" data-audio-player-add-queue-to-playlist aria-label="@localizer["AudioPlayerAddQueueToPlaylist"]">@localizer["PlaylistAddToPlaylist"]</button>
            </div>
            <ul class="audio-player-queue" data-audio-player-queue aria-label="@localizer["AudioPlayerQueue"]"></ul>
        </div>
    </div>
    <!-- Condensed bar: transport controls, three state progress bar, volume, and track name. -->
    <div class="audio-player-bar">
        <img class="audio-player-cover-thumbnail" data-audio-player-cover-thumbnail alt="" />
        <div class="audio-player-track-labels">
            <span class="audio-player-track-name" data-audio-player-track-name></span>
            <span class="audio-player-album-name" data-audio-player-album-name></span>
        </div>
        <span class="audio-player-time audio-player-current-time" data-audio-player-current-time>0:00</span>
        <div class="audio-player-progress" data-audio-player-progress data-audio-player-progress-state="idle" role="slider" tabindex="0"
             aria-label="@localizer["AudioPlayerSeek"]" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="1" aria-valuenow="0" aria-busy="false">
            <div class="audio-player-progress-undownloaded" data-audio-player-progress-undownloaded data-audio-player-progress-layer="undownloaded"></div>
            <div class="audio-player-progress-downloaded" data-audio-player-progress-downloaded data-audio-player-progress-layer="downloaded"></div>
            <div class="audio-player-progress-played" data-audio-player-progress-played data-audio-player-progress-layer="played"></div>
        </div>
        <span class="audio-player-time audio-player-total-time" data-audio-player-total-time>--:--</span>
        <div class="audio-player-queue-controls">
            <button type="button" class="audio-player-button audio-player-previous" data-audio-player-previous aria-label="@localizer["AudioPlayerPrevious"]">
                <span class="audio-player-previous-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="audio-player-button audio-player-play-pause" data-audio-player-play-pause aria-label="@localizer["AudioPlayerPlay"]">
                <span class="audio-player-play-pause-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="audio-player-button audio-player-stop" data-audio-player-stop aria-label="@localizer["AudioPlayerStop"]">
                <span class="audio-player-stop-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="audio-player-button audio-player-next" data-audio-player-next aria-label="@localizer["AudioPlayerNext"]">
                <span class="audio-player-next-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="audio-player-button audio-player-repeat" data-audio-player-repeat data-audio-player-repeat-mode="off"
                    aria-pressed="false" aria-label="@localizer["AudioPlayerRepeatOff"]">
                <span class="audio-player-repeat-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#8635;</span>
                <span class="audio-player-repeat-one-badge" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
            </button>
        </div>
        <div class="audio-player-volume-control">
            <button type="button" class="audio-player-button audio-player-mute" data-audio-player-mute aria-label="@localizer["AudioPlayerMute"]" aria-pressed="false">
                <span class="audio-player-mute-icon"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="audio-player-volume" data-audio-player-volume role="slider" tabindex="0"
                 aria-label="@localizer["AudioPlayerVolume"]" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" aria-valuenow="100">
                <div class="audio-player-volume-level" data-audio-player-volume-level></div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="audio-player-controls">
            <button type="button" id="audio-player-expand-toggle" aria-label="@localizer["ToggleExpanded"]">
                <span class="audio-player-expand-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
